# Keycloak OIDC (wired in Plan 5 Task 2). There is nothing to set here: the frontend reads
# Keycloak settings at runtime from /config.json (src/config.ts), not from a VITE_* build-time
# variable, so one built image can be redeployed against a different Keycloak without a
# rebuild (Plan 8 Task 4).
#
#   - Dev server (`npm run dev`): served statically from frontend/public/config.json. Edit
#     that file directly if your local Keycloak is not at its defaults
#     (http://localhost:8080, realm vocal-coach, client vocal-coach-web).
#   - Compose/production (frontend container): frontend/docker-entrypoint.sh writes
#     /usr/share/nginx/html/config.json from the KEYCLOAK_URL, KEYCLOAK_REALM and
#     KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID environment variables on the `frontend` service in the root
#     docker-compose.yml, which default from the root .env (see the repo root .env.example).
#
# The API is always same-origin at /api (dev server proxy in vite.config.ts, nginx in prod).
